--- body ---
## Context

Reported from padme, 2026-10-30, six landings in one interactive Claude Code
session (padme PRs #175, #177, #179, #180, #181, #182). Each `raid_land.py` run
printed at step 5a:

    attribution: invalid: line 3: fact order requires kind, pr, writer before reviewers (PR body: missing)

The review notes held gaze `reviewer:` lines but no `writer:` entry: only raid
and hunt record one (ticket 1307), and an interactive session that runs gaze,
verify-gate and merge by hand never does. `attribution_record.py --render-pr`
then refuses the block (`scripts/attribution_record.py:94`), the PR body keeps
no attribution, and roar's `--capture-unit` refuses too until a writer line is
added by hand (`--record-writer`, which itself demands step, route and
independence fields). The warning never blocks, so it is easy to ignore on
every landing.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] A landing from an interactive session either records the writer itself
      (merge skill or `raid_land.py`, from the session's runtime and model) or
      renders the reviewer lines without one, but does not print `invalid` for
      the ordinary case
- [ ] Roar's `--capture-unit` works on such a PR without a hand-typed writer line
- [ ] Test: a review on notes with gaze answers and no writer entry lands and
      captures with no `invalid` warning
